# A string or a reader call alone as a query is a table: DS0150 with a machine-applicable fix.
mode: syntax
---- query
'data/orders.csv';
read_parquet('x.parquet')
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..45
  PIPELINE@0..17
    LITERAL@0..17
      STRING@0..17 "'data/orders.csv'"
  SEMICOLON@17..18 ";"
  WHITESPACE@18..19 "\n"
  PIPELINE@19..44
    CALL_EXPR@19..44
      NAME_REF@19..31
        IDENT@19..31 "read_parquet"
      ARG_LIST@31..44
        L_PAREN@31..32 "("
        LITERAL@32..43
          STRING@32..43 "'x.parquet'"
        R_PAREN@43..44 ")"
  WHITESPACE@44..45 "\n"

error[DS0150]: a query starts with `from`
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | 'data/orders.csv';
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ read this table with `from`
  |
  = help: insert `from`: `from 'data/orders.csv'`

error[DS0150]: a query starts with `from`
  --> query:2:1
  |
2 | read_parquet('x.parquet')
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ read this table with `from`
  |
  = help: insert `from`: `from read_parquet('x.parquet')`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'data/orders.csv';
    from read_parquet('x.parquet')
which parses without errors
